  "body": "Effort: low\n\n## What changed\n\n`assets/machines/fehlmann-picomax55.mch`:\n\n- X, Y and Z state `travel`: X -500..500, Y -255..255, Z -147..147 mm.\n- The head spindle states `rigid_tapping: true` (the machine owner confirms it).\n- The description names \"the machine parameters\" and no parameter file.\n\n## Readings and choices\n\n- Travel zero point: the file format says a slide of stroke L is written -L..L (the full stroke each way from the work origin). The manual gives only the strokes: X 500, Y 255, Z (quill) 147 mm. The file follows that rule and the other shipped files.\n- Spindle mount: SF32 is not in `SPINDLE_MOUNTS` and the holder library has no SF32 holders yet (#3919 waits for measurements). So `tooling.spindle_mount` stays out. The description says why.\n- Max spindle speed stays 9000. This machine has the 9000 rpm spindle. The manual lists 7100 for the standard spindle.\n- No maximum tap size is stored. The manual's M20 is for steel 700 N/mm2. The capacity depends on the material.\n- Feed rates are unchanged.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `machine_controller`: `mounting_saving_and_reopening_the_picomax_preserves_its_installation` (updated: states the travel).\n- `machine_controller`: `the_picomax_states_travel_and_rigid_tapping_and_no_parameter_file_name` (new).\n- `machine_controller`: `a_face_wider_than_the_picomax_x_stroke_is_refused_naming_the_op_and_the_stroke` (new: a face wider than the X stroke is refused by name).\n- Posted output unchanged: Heidenhain post suites (`klartext_builtin`, `script_heidenhain_klartext`) and `example_catalog*`. Results are in the gate log.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No heavy lanes. No machine run.\n- The Y and Z strokes have no own refusal test. They use the same travel law as X.\n\nChangelog: Fehlmann Picomax 55 machine file states its travel limits and rigid tapping.\n\nFixes #4396\n",
